%% alt: Sequence diagram comparing when the schema is checked. With schema-on-write, the store checks every new listing at insert time and rejects a bad one, so the consumer later reads clean rows. With schema-on-read, the store saves whatever it receives, and the consumer must check for missing keys and wrong types while reading.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant P as Producer
  participant S as Store
  participant C as Consumer
  alt Schema-on-write, a database table
    P->>S: insert listing, rent = "negotiable"
    Note over S: check the schema NOW<br/>rent must be a number
    S-->>P: rejected
    P->>S: insert listing, rent = 415
    S-->>P: accepted
    C->>S: SELECT AVG(rent)
    S-->>C: clean rows, same columns
  else Schema-on-read, JSON documents
    P->>S: save whatever it has
    Note over S: no check at the door
    S-->>P: saved
    C->>S: read the documents
    S-->>C: raw documents
    Note over C: check the schema NOW<br/>missing keys? wrong types?
  end
